  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Men and women, especially the youth and other groups at  risk of vulnerability or marginalization, acquire appropriate competencies and have access to and engage in remunerative and productive work.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PHL 101 supports the Philippine Labor and Employment Plan (LEP) 2023 to 2028, contributing to Priority 1 on maximizing productive, remunerative, freely chosen, and sustainable work. It aims to increase employability, expand access to employment, and promote shared labour market governance. The strategy strengthens active labour market programs (ALMPs), skills development, and labour market information systems (LMIS), targeting youth, women, and vulnerable groups. It also aligns with the National Technical Education and Skills Development Plan (NTESDP) 2023 to 2028, advancing modern, inclusive, and high-quality technical and vocational education and training (TVET). It contributes to labour statistics development, including pilots on the new work concept, informal economy, green jobs supporting the Philippine Statistical Development Program (PSDP) 2023 to 2029.

Key interventions include enhancing employment opportunities for youth in the ASEAN construction sector by building regional and national capacities to provide relevant digital and green skills; supporting the Global Accelerator through skills needs anticipation in priority sectors, particularly construction and transportation; supporting the Trabaho para sa Bayan plan to support evidence-based policy formulation and guide education and training institutions in responding to current and future labour market demands; and operationalizing the green transition at the sector level through the development of sector skills plans based on the Green Jobs Human Resource Development Plan. The CPO also supports the assessment of youth employability programmes to generate evidence-based recommendations that improve their effectiveness, inclusiveness, and alignment with national development priorities. 

It contributes to the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF) 2024 to 2028, particularly Output 1 on inclusive, resilient, and quality learning environment and Outcome 2 on decent work.</narrative>
  </description>
